`nxc guide` is chat's own guide verb — one of the three building blocks' (6j6v.9e3r), sharing the
mechanism `nxf guide` and `nxm guide` use. It needs no workspace: the content is compiled into the
binary.

Seven topics (6j6v.t6vd, and `writing-declarations` from 6j6v.9w08), in the order they are meant
to be read.

```console
$ nxc guide
Guides (run `nxc guide <topic>`):

  getting-started       Activate chat, declare a persona, and get your first answer back.
  core-concepts         The shared op-log, qualified handles, threads and their derived quorum, and how a message is delivered.
  commands              Every shipped verb, with its `--json` shape — and what was removed, with what to do instead.
  personas              Declaring one agent: identity, prompt layers, model band, tools, and who may address it.
  channels              Declaring a group — and the ordered channel (`flow: sequential`) that IS the workflow.
  writing-declarations  From an intention to a declaration that answers usefully: seven measured error classes, and a checklist.
  limits-and-safety     The hop cap, the human gate, the working-copy lease, and what an agent does NOT decide.

```

The `--json` listing shape is identical across the blocks (`[{summary, topic}]`), so a caller that
learned it from `nxf guide --json` already knows this one. The ORDER is part of the contract.

```console
$ nxc guide --json
[{"summary":"Activate chat, declare a persona, and get your first answer back.","topic":"getting-started"},{"summary":"The shared op-log, qualified handles, threads and their derived quorum, and how a message is delivered.","topic":"core-concepts"},{"summary":"Every shipped verb, with its `--json` shape — and what was removed, with what to do instead.","topic":"commands"},{"summary":"Declaring one agent: identity, prompt layers, model band, tools, and who may address it.","topic":"personas"},{"summary":"Declaring a group — and the ordered channel (`flow: sequential`) that IS the workflow.","topic":"channels"},{"summary":"From an intention to a declaration that answers usefully: seven measured error classes, and a checklist.","topic":"writing-declarations"},{"summary":"The hop cap, the human gate, the working-copy lease, and what an agent does NOT decide.","topic":"limits-and-safety"}]

```

A topic this block does not carry is a `validation` error naming what IS on offer — never a silent
empty answer. `workflow` is the interesting case: it was a verb group until 6j6v.dvyq §3, and what
replaced it is a channel that declares its order, so the honest answer points at `channels`.

```console
$ nxc guide workflow --json
? 1
{"error":{"kind":"validation","msg":"unknown guide topic 'workflow'; expected one of getting-started, core-concepts, commands, personas, channels, writing-declarations, limits-and-safety"}}

```
